                    <view key="view" autoresizesSubviews="NO" contentMode="top" id="9Ac-If-LoR">
                        <rect key="frame" x="0.0" y="0.0" width="820" height="1180"/>
                        <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMaxY="YES"/>
                        <subviews>
                            <textView clipsSubviews="YES" multipleTouchEnabled="YES" contentMode="scaleToFill" fixedFrame="YES" showsHorizontalScrollIndicator="NO" editable="NO" selectable="NO" translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints="NO" id="zWr-CC-nc6">
                                <rect key="frame" x="20" y="72" width="728" height="234"/>
                                <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMaxY="YES"/>
                                <color key="backgroundColor" red="1" green="1" blue="1" alpha="1" colorSpace="custom" customColorSpace="sRGB"/>
                                <string key="text">1.   Cards must alternate colors in the lower four stacks and count down.
2.   Cards must be of the same suit in the upper four stacks and count up.
3.   Click on the deck to get three cards at a time.
4.   There are 13 face-up cards above the deck (the "blind").
5.    A King is "below" an Ace, and a Two is "above" an Ace.  
6.    Upper stacks must start with the card dealt.
7.    Empty lower stacks may only be filled with cards from the blind.
8.    If the blind is empty, gaps may be filled with a card that is one below the card dealt to the upper stack.
9.    $5 is awarded for each card placed in an upper stack.
10.  Winning the game gains you $250.
11.  Auto moves any available card to an upper stack.
12.  Auto actions *cannot* be undone.</string>
                                <fontDescription key="fontDescription" type="system" pointSize="14"/>
                                <textInputTraits key="textInputTraits" autocapitalizationType="sentences"/>
                            </textView>
